> What's the usual inventory management strategy? Throwing every potion
> to enemies to try the identification? Not taking gems or scrolls until
> I have a way of identifying them?
>
If you know of a store you can sell stuff to, you can usually price id
and keep the stuff you need around, and stash the other stuff away.
scrolls are pretty light, and you should have no problem carrying them
around.  the potions end up being quite heavy though.  at least until
you find a special bag (try uncursing the one you found on the
corpse).
You can basically identify gems as you get them by trying to engrave
with them.  they only weigh 1 each anyway, so they're probably not
what's slowing you down.  rocks and gray stones though...

basically, anything that won't immediately save you, or you won't need
in a hurry is something you should stash.  gold detection scrolls,
blank scrolls, stuff like that you don't really need to carry around,
as they're usually not something you need right away.

